Critical findings / analysis:
- Backend route `/api/admin/export/transcripts` is correctly protected with `isAdmin` and validates both selector dimensions (`type` and `id`) with strict allowed values.
- Export logic covers required workbook structure: per-user sheets, sanitized sheet names (invalid chars replaced, 31-char cap, duplicate suffixing), styled header row, 4 required columns, message text wrapping, and PST-labeled timestamps.
- Conversation handling is correct: users can include multiple records; each record’s messages are included in chronological order; message numbering resets per conversation; divider rows are inserted when multiple records exist.
- User sheet ordering is deterministic via username/email sorting, and users with no messages are skipped.
- Frontend card is implemented with the 6 fixed options, loading state on button, and destructive error toast on failure.
- Filename formatting is descriptive and aligned with requirement intent (`session-transcripts-<foundation|enhancement>-<id>-YYYY-MM-DD.xlsx`).

